{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["html","css","js"],"cmd":[],"ctl":"worqhm1a15dab50e4m2d2b","db":"dev","desc":"THE 3D flow editor (the Development app mounts it for #/flow/<lib>/<ctlId>/<cmdId>; dev.floweditor3d is now just a delegate to it). Built on the app scene stack: ops are app:scenehost-hosted dev:flownode instances whose click/drag behaviors are the wiring gestures (port tap, wire ghost, keyboard W/arrows/Enter, I-1/I-2 enforced); the FlowDoc stays authoritative and the scene facet is a derived view (flowproject.toSceneDoc). Props {title, graph, source:{lib,ctl,cmd}, onBack}; with no props it runs as the gate harness. Authoring: palette (primitive/command/local/constant/persistent/blank) create + splice, op/terminal/signature inspector, delete op, case chain add/remove, tidy/untangle layout, undo/redo, diagnostics. Save = write_flow_body with base-hash → stale_base → conflict. Run ▸ (or R) hosts one dev:flowtoken per wire in flowdoc.propagationRounds order and, with a source, invokes the real saved command with an args form. STEP DEBUGGER (flow step debugger P4, in progress): debug ⏯ (or F11/F10) opens a dev.flowstep debug session on the CURRENT, unsaved body (args form for params); toolbar + keys F11 into, F10 over, ⇧F11 out, F5 continue (polled; pause), ⇧F10 back, ⇧F5 stop; the focus follows the top frame (drills into local frames, shows the case it runs); op state rides dev:flownode plates (ready/running/done/skipped), wire and synchro state is tinted on the facade, and a tap on a READY op/wire/synchro runs it next; every step SHOWS what it moved - each delivery rides its wire on a dev:flowtoken, a fired synchro pulses, a next rule rides the jump pipe, a drill flies the orbit to the local op - and back(1) plays the undone event in reverse (debugLastRide reports it); edits are locked while a session is open; the mapping lives in dev:flowdebug. While debugging the INSPECTOR is the debugger's: the frame stack top first (click a frame = focus its case; the focus follows the top frame again on the next move or 'follow the top frame'), the ready set as pick buttons, the selected op's inputs (value + delivered mark) and outputs/results, a selected wire's source and delivered values, a synchro's state, and the focused frame's args and out (debugInspector = the model, debugInspectorDom = the rendered rows, debugFocusFrame/debugFollowNow). Otherwise the inspector shows unsaved changes (diffFlow) and the server journal (diff + revert). api includes dispose, startRun/runLive, startDebug/debugStep/debugStop/debugView/debugFrames/debugLastRide/debugInspector, addDeck/removeDeck, selectOp/selectWire/walkOps/frameSelection, serialize, baseHash.","groups":"anonymous","id":"worqhm1a15dab50e4m2d2b","lib":"dev","name":"flowedit3d"},"id":"worqhm1a15dab50e4m2d2b","readers":[],"time":1792788721444,"username":"system","writers":[]}